		<help>
			<key>
				<name>]</name>
				<desc>Start engines</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>[</name>
				<desc>Shut down engines</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>R</name>
				<desc>Toggle rotor brake</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>Ctrl d</name>
				<desc>Turn off SAS</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>r</name>
				<desc>Activate the Rescue Winch man</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>q</name>
				<desc>Rotate Searchlight Up</desc>
			</key>
			<key>
				<name>a</name>
				<desc>Rotate Searchlight Left</desc>
			</key>
			<key>
				<name>z</name>
				<desc>Rotate Searchlight Down</desc>
			</key>
			<key>
				<name>d</name>
				<desc>Rotate Searchlight Right</desc>
			</key>
			<line>If you are using HDR, then you need to enable the specific HDR panel lights from the BK117 Menu.</line>
 <line>Using the HDR panel lights while not in HDR will produce very strange results.</line>
			<line> </line>
			<line></line>
			<line> MTOW is 7385lb. Fast Cruise is 130kts. VNE 150kts</line>
			<line></line>
			<line>Landing light + Search light ( when fitted ) are switched on/off from the switches on the collective.</line>
			<line> The Rescue Winch man is only available on configurations which include the winch. He is only viewable once he is active and the right  sliding door is open </line>
			<line></line>
			<line>Emergancy floats are armed by the toggle switch on the centre console. This is only available when the floats are configured on the Helicopter</line>
			<line> The floats are inflated by pressing the red button on the collective. Again this is only available once the floats are configured on the Helicopter.</line>
			<line></line>
			<line> SAR Menu option - THIS IS JUST A FUN   MULTIPLAYER FEATURE !!</line>
			<line> If you crash your BK117, you can use this menu option to call on another BK117,</line>
			<line>or any other chopper running the script, to retrieve your broken chopper and you, as an underslung load.</line>
		<line> </line>
<line>AUTOPILOT V3 </line>
<line>The Autopilot is now able to control  speed, altitude and heading. Autopilot is only usable  between 30-140kts</line>
<line>Heading modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>Speed modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>****  Altitude modes can only be used in conjunction with speed mode being being active. This includes the use of Vertical Speed mode.  ***</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT ISSUES !!!!!</line>
<line>When disengaging the AP entirely or from a singe mode, the  control inputs will snap to your actual cyclic/colective/pedal positions as soon as you  move any of them.</line>
<line>This is unavoidable as  the sim can not physically move your cyclic/colective/pedal positions to match the Autopilots input.</line>
<line>The best advice to minimise the sudden change of input would be for you to  have your cyclic/colective/pedal positions ready in approximatly correct positions  to minimise the "snap".</line>

		
		</help>

		<hitches>
			<!-- make sure some properties do exist, when the list for multiplayer transfere is defined-->
			<!-- they need to be in the same value, as they are initilized in the FDM, to get the same values after reset
    should fix this somehow-->
